{"name":"Casual Day","hex":"#95bac2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"casual","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Happening by chance.","Coming without regularity; occasional or incidental."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A worker who is only working for a company occasionally, not as its permanent employee.","A worker who is doing a particular type of job temporarily, not as a lifetime career."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casual"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Casual Day","blocks":[{"text":"Casual Day is a 2007 Spanish dark workplace comedy film directed by Max Lemcke. The ensemble cast features Juan Diego, Luis Tosar, Estíbaliz Gabilondo, Arturo Valls, Alberto San Juan, Malena Alterio, Álex Angulo, Carlos Kaniowsky, Secun de la Rosa, Marta Etura and Mikel Losada."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Casual_Day_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casual_Day","wikidata":"Q5661779"},{"title":"Casual Friday","blocks":[{"text":"Casual Friday is a Western dress code trend in which businesses relax their dress code on Fridays. Businesses that usually require employees to wear suits, dress shirts, neckties, and dress shoes, may allow more casual or business casual wear on such days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Casual_Friday.jpg/330px-Casual_Friday.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casual_Friday","wikidata":"Q1049995"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_2.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_2.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_2.jpg/500px-Mid